MLLM description: Abyssinian cats are known for their distinctive physical features, including a slender body, large ears, and a short, dense coat with a "ticked" pattern. Their coloration is typically a rich golden or reddish-brown, with darker points on the ears, face, paws, and tail. They have a medium-sized head with a slightly rounded forehead and a long, narrow muzzle. Abyssinians are medium-sized cats, with males being larger than females. They are known for their playful and energetic nature, often engaging in interactive play with their owners. Their unique identifying trait is their ticked coat pattern, which gives them a distinct appearance compared to other cat breeds.
